Explanation of the new regex bits:

- `(?:_?\d)*` or `(?:[\da-fA-F]_?)+` allow any number of underscores between valid digit characters.
- We mirror that logic in hex (`0[xX]…`), binary (`0[bB]…`), octal (`0[oO]…`), decimal/floats/exponents, and optional BigInt `n` suffix.
- All other parts of each file remain untouched.
